Z||000007||California Kid||07-18-2001||11:05 PM||||Hey this is a "Taboo" subject, not too many people like to admit how much they have thrown into their toy, because they know that they're most likely not to get it back. I will admit that my ballpark total is under $25,000. Haven't had the car appraised yet, so I don't really know what it's worth. The only satisfaction is that I know it will out perform any production car under $100,000.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever2||07-18-2001||11:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I have nearly as much in the car as I paid for it. and it still has the original motor!!<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Same here, I bought this car... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/003807.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/003807.html</A> <BR>...for $3000, and have spent about that amount on it since.  If I had been able to do my own work on the expensive things, it would be a different story.  But at the time, I was just starting to learn about Fieros.<P>My black 88 GT was purchased for $5000 in perfect condition, but after I wrecked it, it sat in the garage for 19 months.  Now I am driving it again, but it <I>needs</I> that much put into it.  I just don't have it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||skitime||07-18-2001||11:28 PM||||I don't want to even keep track of it any more.  It was money well spent I hope. Still  a lot less than almost every other good looking sports car out there. All of the work I have done myself except the paint so that keeps costs down. Still I am probably under $7000<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080039-2_4.jpg"> ||||reg||1
