Z||000013||Ferrari_cdn||07-19-2001||12:49 AM||||jeez.  that sounds like you guys spend a lot of money.  My 57,000 km '84 Fiero 2M4 with engine rebuilt, I hope I don't have to shell out that much money over a few years...<P>My bro in law's uncle said he never had major trouble with the car.||||reg||4
Z||000014||AusFiero||07-19-2001||01:32 AM||||Well I know the Australian dollar is only a Peso compared to the American dollar but I have over $32,000 tied up in my NEAR STOCK Fiero. Or about $17,000 US at current exchange rates. <P>The government got lots of that in import duties on parts etc because we pay between 25 to 52% import duties here in Aus. Also I did pay a little more for some parts local I coulda got in myself but lets face it, when you want a part it is easier to drive 15 minutes to the parts importer (friend of mine that looks after me well, owns <A HREF="http://www.pontiworld.com" TARGET=_blank>Ponti-World</A>)than to wait weeks from another country and maybe get the wrong part.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Monkeyman||07-19-2001||03:02 AM||||I'm too scared to look and see what I have in 4Play already, but I figure I'll have somewhere between 15k and 20k in her before I'm done.  For that money, I should have a basically brand new car so I feel it will be money well spent.  I'd spend a hell of a lot less if I learned to do my own work.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
