Z||000026||Fformula88||07-19-2001||08:47 PM||||I've put about $4000-$4500 into the car including purchase price since I bought it in.  I've added another $1000 in extra's, but I don't really consider it part of the operating cost.<P>Another question... who is also supporting another car?  My Fiero isn't my daily driver, so I am putting money into two vehicles.  Somehow, they both always need oil changes, tires, and other things at the same time.  They must conspire against me!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000027||Formula||07-19-2001||09:15 PM||||I bought the car for $1500 and I have about $7000 into it now from this motor swap...<P>it looks better then a new $20,000 car and it should run better then a new $20,000 car. 'nough said...<P>(assuming that V6 mustang and camaros are still in the 20k price range)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000028||terryk||07-20-2001||12:37 AM||||About $4500 total on my red 86SE with the 3800SC including the car. ||||reg||1
