Z||000030||AusFiero||07-20-2001||01:22 AM||||Hey Roger. Your car isn't exactly a stock Fiero though is it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Is quite nice though.<P>I think Coolblue is right. This is a horrible subject to think about. If I add the tow car to take the family to shows with me well then we can add another $36,000.<P>But what the hell. Its money, we make it to live and enjoy it. Might as well enjoy it on something we like hey  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I will be better prepared next time around, had to pay to get things done I coulda done myself due to too much time running the business. Thats all changed now.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000031||stsmithgt||07-20-2001||10:03 AM||||I've spent about 7,000 and counting, but some of that is from repairing damage from a hungry Cadillac.  It ate a door, fender and some suspension.  It still has an exhaust leak on the front manifold I'm looking into.  Everything is so expensive, I'm slowly checking the options out there to fix the leak for good. (I hope)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000032||onfire||07-20-2001||12:54 PM||||So far just $2000 for the car. I will have another $2000 in wheels tires and bigger brakes, by xmas hopefully. After xmas comes the 4.9 caddy swap, $600 for the motor and $1000 or so for my friend to rebuild it. And help install it. Plus more money for interior, and exterior work. <P>I also have an 86 s10 4x4 that gets alot of my money. Up next is new shocks and a 2" lift. The motor I fear will need a rebuild sometime next year. My uncle said he would do it for about $750 including parts. I wanna take the seats out of the Fiero and put them in my truck, with Mr. Mikes leather of course. So the Fiero will need new seats. Ahhh a never ending cycle.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
